Subject: [PATCH] Port to the wasm64 lean4game build (Lean 4.33.0-pre, Mathlib
 de3a9cf)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Import layer (no level or world removed, nothing a player types changed):
- Game/Data.lean: drop 22 Mathlib.Data.* imports that are not in the essential Mathlib
  pack (none is used by any level); follow the Data.Matrix -> LinearAlgebra.Matrix
  and Data.Real.{Cardinality,Sqrt} -> Analysis.Real.* moves; import
  Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.VectorSpace so the root `VectorSpace` namespace that
  every level's `open VectorSpace` relies on stays in the closure.
- InnerProductWorld/LemmasAndDefs.lean: drop `Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.AbsMax`
  (245-module closure outside the pack; `Complex.abs` only appears in comments) and
  use Mathlib.Analysis.Real.Sqrt directly (Data.Real.Sqrt is a deprecated shim).
- Game.lean: `Languages "English"` -> `Languages "en"`; the Tutorial -> VectorSpace
  `Dependency` moves here because the current GameServer rejects a source world that
  is not imported by the file declaring the edge (VectorSpaceWorld.lean does not
  import TutorialWorld).

Mathlib drift (taught names kept as aliases of the identical statements):
- `MulAction.mul_smul` -> `SemigroupAction.mul_smul` in the VectorSpaceWorld/Level01
  inventory (players type `mul_smul`, which still resolves).
- `alias Finset.sum_eq_sum_diff_singleton_add := Finset.sum_eq_sum_sdiff_singleton_add`
  (LIS Level08; the old additive name was removed upstream).
- `alias sq_eq_sq := sq_eq_sq₀` (InnerProductWorld Level03).

Proof drift (`field_simp` rewrite, unused simp args):
- InnerProductWorld Level06: the taught `field_simp [h_nonzero]` now leaves
  `⟪u,v⟫ * (1 - 1) = 0`; the level closes with an extra `ring` step (hint added).
- LemmasAndDefs.ortho_decom_parts: `ring` after `field_simp`; Level07 helper
  `norm_sq_scaled_eq`: redundant `ring` removed; Level07 `simp [div_mul_cancel,
  v_norm_zero] at h_mul` -> `simp [v_norm_zero] at h_mul` (unused arg, hint updated);
  two unused simp arguments dropped in LemmasAndDefs helper proofs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
