+-- wasm64 port: Mathlib removed `sq_eq_sq` (it was a deprecated alias of `sq_eq_sq₀`); keep the name
+-- this level teaches as an alias of the same statement.
+alias _root_.sq_eq_sq := sq_eq_sq₀
+
 /--
 `sq_eq_sq` is a proof that if `a` and `b` are nonnegative, `a^2 = b^2` if and only if `a = b`. If you
 have hypotheses `h1 : 0 ≤ a`, `h2 : 0 ≤ b`, then `sq_eq_sq h1 h2` is a proof that `a ^ 2 = b ^ 2 ↔ a = b`.
